---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Security"
  description="How WizardLoop separates its static website from feedback services, protects credentials and receives private vulnerability reports."
>
  <section class="wrap prose-page">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">BUILT WITH CARE</p>
      <h1>
        Small surface.
        <br />
        Clear boundaries.
      </h1>
      <p>
        Security is part of maintaining this personal website. This page
        describes the design and its practical limits.
      </p>
      <p>
        Reviewed <time datetime="2026-10-27">27 October 2026</time>.
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>The website and its services</h2>
      <p>
        The main website is a static site hosted on GitHub Pages. It does not
        require visitor accounts or passwords. Fonts and core visual assets are
        served with the site. Optional third-party content is separated from the
        main reading experience.
      </p>
      <p>
        Feedback uses a separate Cloudflare Worker when configured. That service
        validates form fields on the server, verifies Turnstile, checks the
        exact request origin and challenge hostname, limits request size and
        submission rate, and escapes content before sending it to Telegram. A
        missing required security configuration makes the service unavailable.
      </p>
      <p>
        Bot credentials, secret keys and private destination identifiers belong
        in server-side secret storage. They are not included in the public
        website build. The local feedback mock does not send Telegram messages
        and identifies its results as local tests.
      </p>

      <h2>What these measures do not guarantee</h2>
      <p>
        No website can promise complete protection. Third-party services have
        their own availability, security and data-handling rules. A feedback
        request can fail, and a network timeout can leave delivery uncertain.
        The form reports that uncertainty instead of claiming success.
      </p>
      <p>
        GitHub Pages does not provide arbitrary per-site HTTP response-header
        configuration. Controls that require response headers cannot all be
        enabled through site source alone. This page does not claim that a
        configurable CSP, Permissions Policy or other CDN-level protection is
        active on the main site. Additional controls would require a separately
        reviewed hosting or proxy configuration.
      </p>
      <p>
        The separate feedback API sets its own restrictive response headers.
        Those headers do not change the headers served by GitHub Pages.
        Production deployment and infrastructure changes require a separate
        review.
      </p>

      <h2>Report a vulnerability privately</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href="mailto:wizard@wizardloop.com">wizard@wizardloop.com</a>{' '}
        with a concise description, the affected URL or component, and safe
        steps to reproduce the issue. You can also{' '}
        <a href="https://t.me/wizardloop">contact me on Telegram</a> to arrange
        a private report.
      </p>
      <p>
        Please do not post secrets, personal data or exploit details in a public
        issue. Use your own test data, avoid service disruption and stop if a
        test exposes someone else's information. There is no promised
        response-time guarantee or paid bounty program.
      </p>
      <p>
        The source and security guidance are available in the{' '}
        <a href="https://github.com/WizardLoop/wizardloop.github.io">
          website repository
        </a>
        . Public code is available for review; access to source is not
        permission to test third-party infrastructure.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
